 "steps": [
  {
   "caption": "The relation is a cycle: a → b, b → c, c → a. Row x has a mark in column y when R(x, y) holds.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "g",
     "set": {
      "highlight": [
       [
        1,
        2
       ],
       [
        2,
        3
       ],
       [
        3,
        1
       ]
      ]
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "∀x∃y R(x, y): for each row, can we find a mark? Row a: column b. Row b: column c. Row c: column a. Yes, every row has one.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "b1",
     "set": {
      "label": "∀x∃y R(x, y) = T",
      "tone": "success",
      "fill": "success"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "∃y∀x R(x, y): is some column full? Each column has exactly one mark, so no single y works for every x.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "b2",
     "set": {
      "label": "∃y∀x R(x, y) = F",
      "tone": "danger",
      "fill": "danger"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "g",
     "set": {
      "highlight": [
       [
        1,
        1
